exports[`renderHumanReport — doctor and uninstall > renders checks with a severity marker and a fix 1`] = `
"paseo-bm 0.1.0 — doctor (read-only, nothing is written)
Paseo CLI 0.8.0, daemon 0.8.0, home /fake/home/.paseo, plugins enabled: yes

Checks
  [ok]    paseo-cli      Paseo CLI 0.8.0 and daemon 0.8.0 agree.
  [error] plugin-status  The paseo-bm plugin is registered but its status is disabled.
                         Fix: Run \`npx paseo-bm install --apply\` and consent to enabling plugins.
  [warn]  skills         codex is missing 1 of 2 required skills.
                         Fix: Run the printed \`skills add\` command.

1 ok, 1 warning, 1 error

Agent roles
  manager   claude/opus-5      Paseo tools: yes; signed in: yes
  worker    codex/gpt-5.6-sol  Paseo tools: yes; signed in: no
  reviewer  codex/gpt-5.6-sol  Paseo tools: no; signed in: unknown

Agent skills
  source: cuongntr/agent-skills
  claude: 2 present, none missing
  codex: 1 present, missing: implementing-beads
  run it yourself: npx -y skills add cuongntr/agent-skills --agent codex implementing-beads

Warnings (these never change the exit code)
  W_PROVIDER_NOT_LOGGED_IN  The provider chosen for an agent role has no active login session, so that role cannot start a session yet.
    worker uses codex
    Fix: Run that tool's own login command — paseo-bm never handles credentials — then run \`paseo-bm doctor\` to confirm. The role stays registered either way.

Plugin status: disabled
Exit code 1 — doctor found drift in what paseo-bm owns
"
`;

